# Paths whose `vibeic-eda:X.Y.Z` references are HISTORY, not live pointers.
# One glob per line. See sync_image_version.py — a live pointer must move with
# VERSION; a historical one must not, because rewriting it states that a
# measurement was taken against a version it was not taken against.

# Every reference in this file is of the form
#     Measured: `ls /foss/tools` in `ghcr.io/vibeic/vibeic-eda:0.2.31`  (image-version:history — this line is the EXAMPLE, not a pointer)
# — it records WHICH IMAGE WAS INSPECTED to produce the tables below it. Bumping
# those to the current version would claim the inventory was re-measured when it
# was not. There is no install command anywhere in the file (checked: zero
# `docker pull` / `docker run` lines), so nothing here is a pointer a reader
# would copy.
#
# Registered 2026-07-30 while cutting 0.2.46; the two references had been at
# 0.2.31 since before that and were failing --check as "unregistered".
docs/TOOL_INVENTORY.md

# `Dockerfile` — PATH-level on purpose, not the per-line marker.
#
# The root Dockerfile is an INPUT TO THE IMAGE: `compose_recipe_hash` digests it
# whole, comments included, deliberately (a comment-only edit used not to move the
# fingerprint, and that was the hole #19/#20 fixed). So editing it to add a
# marker invalidates RELEASED.json until the next real build — measured, by doing
# exactly that: the 0.2.56 record stopped reproducing (c2b9b8b9a843 vs
# 3a0b5d567c32) and `check_release_recorded` failed.
#
# A file that may not be touched cannot carry an inline opt-out, so the exemption
# has to be the path. The cost is low and checkable: every live image reference in
# this file is `eda-tool-*` or the `hpretl/...` base, never `vibeic-eda:X.Y.Z` —
# a version of ours appears here only as the SUBJECT of a measurement.
Dockerfile
